  "known_local_policies": [
    "A passive portal occupies one normal board slot, appends at the end and is not a summoned character. It runs only its own controller end-turn body; full-board opening leaves any previous successful binding unchanged.",
    "Each successful native opening binds the original still-live residence to that exact portal through an ordinary removable attachment. Repeated Battlecry replaces that binding only after successful installation. Current copies retain the link; ordinary base/bounce resets clear it.",
    "An explicit foreign link cannot use either the enemy portal or an unrelated friendly portal. An unbound summoned/base Sargeras looks for the earliest friendly portal at skill-body time. Exact entry-versus-use fallback and multiple-portal priority are local policies pending calibration.",
    "All three skills are consumed normally when no qualifying portal exists and have no body effect. To the Void removes all other active ordinary board minions in one existing nondeath-removal batch, without Deathrattle/Reborn.",
    "Legion adds an ordinary unit to the selected physical portal. Each unit grants future Imp/Infernal summons +2 Health and Taunt before summon publication; old demons are unchanged. Current copies and ordinary silhouette/base resets follow the existing attachment lifecycle.",
    "Skill work uses the original accepted actor; a later source departure does not undo accepted removal or portal work. Exact control/reaction windows remain locally recorded and are not a completion blocker."
  ]
